          1007.0,
          1472.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "633e861b4f53917096851df28b2da45db1db6ba7a5961bcab2323d371d89c4a2"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This is the genetic variance across the entire population (across all the lines present in generation T). For a pure-line cross, this reduces to",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b11"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          132.0,
          656.0,
          903.0,
          704.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "7e7cf5263185e694748e1dd2163813d76ae7c2c66506945363bb3f5a0303e551"
    },
    {
      "type": "derivation",
      "content": "$$ \\sigma {G}(T,T,T)=(1+f {T})\\sigma {A}^{2}+(1-f {T})(1+f {T})\\sigma {D}^{2} $$",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b12"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          309.0,
          722.0,
          726.0,
          749.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "2bd2922d34bf7481faf5dc6c9e5e506847e25b4f73dbba87c7726a8448edb684"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "We also require the genetic variance in generation T among the subset of lines that descend from a single individual in generation t. Here, $ \\tau = T $ and the variance becomes",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b14"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          132.0,
          767.0,
          904.0,
          815.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "d1f40d9c62a9a78c8b734462027b3b0e8b2ed80d4108938b276fcc253df4fea4"
    },
    {
      "type": "derivation",
      "content": "$$ \\begin{aligned}\\sigma {G}(T,T,t)=(1+f {t})\\sigma {A}^{2}+\\frac{(1-f {T})^{2}}{1-f {t}}\\sigma {D}^{2}+(f {t}+f {T})\\sigma {ADI}\\\\+\\left(f {t}+\\frac{(f {T}-f {t})^{2}}{2(1-f {t})}\\right)\\sigma {DI}^{2}+\\frac{f {t}(1-f {T})^{2}}{1-f {t}}\\iota^{ }\\end{aligned} $$",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b15"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          248.0,
          836.0,
          749.0,
          937.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "90beebe4db1cc8b629a8168592d2e4f47cf3a5fa3de03a59d1a8dafb2559490a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "An example of this would be the genetic variance across the collection of $ F 3 $ or $ F 4 $ bulk families from a single $ F 2 $ parent. For an $ F 3 $ family this is $ \\sigma G(1,1,0) $, as the $ F 2 $ represents generation 0 of selfing, while the entire collection of $ F 4 $ families that trace back to this $ F 2 $ individual has a variance of $ \\sigma G(2,2,0) $. For the selfed offspring from a pure-line cross, Equation 23.36a simplifies to",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b17"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          133.0,
          954.0,
          904.0,
          1072.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "d6edaaa098458a2d1f1c579fbbe45b6b658253e2f84f2c14afd5cf9bb898711b"
    },
    {
      "type": "derivation",
      "content": "$$ \\sigma {G}(T,T,t)=(1+f {t})\\sigma {A}^{2}+\\frac{(1-f {T})^{2}}{1-f {t}}\\left(1+f {t}\\right)\\sigma {D}^{2} $$",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b18"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          309.0,
          1090.0,
          727.0,
          1141.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "3117756697421f1ff0f4e31a7732e72f8ed597b1f83de418961bf0473f178276"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The permanent selection response is given by the covariance between a completely inbred $ F {\\infty} $ line ( $ f {\\infty} = 1 $) and a relative (for example, from the selection unit) in generation $ \\tau $ who last both shared a relative in generation t (as would occur if remnant seed from t was used to form the new lines). Here, Equation 23.32 reduces to",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b2"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          131.0,
          207.0,
          904.0,
          300.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "0faead7ef7aceb632ac1e1ecfa69ca0caf5c1c075d08376fa8bc0dfd891a197f"
    },
    {
      "type": "derivation",
      "content": "$$ \\begin{aligned}\\sigma {G}(\\infty,\\tau,t)&=(1+f {t})\\sigma {A}^{2}+\\frac{1+2f {t}+f {\\tau}}{2}\\sigma {ADI}+\\frac{f {t}+f {\\tau}}{2}\\sigma {DI}^{2}\\\\&\\quad+(1+f {t})^{2}\\sigma {AA}^{2}+(1+f {t})^{3}\\sigma {AAA}^{2}+\\cdots(1+f {t})^{k}\\sigma {A^{k}}^{2}\\end{aligned} $$",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b3"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          244.0,
          317.0,
          790.0,
          394.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "8f9d2782d16f39d94a174d91f59bef06b214e629e55a88cdffaa00576a5bdb0a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "For offspring resulting from selfing a pure-line cross, $ \\sigma {ADI} = \\sigma {DI}^2 = 0 $, leaving the permanent response as only a function of the additive (and additive epistatic) effects,",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b5"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          132.0,
          411.0,
          904.0,
          460.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "coverage_repair": "authoritative_chapter_pdf_source_block",
      "content_sha256": "23f33e383aa9ccf495754af81366e9df9701b5d837888f3363b02be8736a7694"
    },
    {
      "type": "derivation",
      "content": "$$ \\sigma {G}(\\infty,\\tau,t)=(1+f {t})\\sigma {A}^{2}+(1+f {t})^{2}\\sigma {A A}^{2}+\\cdots(1+f {t})^{k}\\sigma {A^{k}}^{2} $$",
      "source_page": 833,
      "source_pages": [
        833
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p027:b6"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          268.0,
