    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Finally, it will prove useful to decompose the total genetic covariance, $ \\sigma_G(T,t) $, into within- and among-family covariances, $ \\sigma_{Gw}(T,t) $ and $ \\sigma_{Gb}(T,t) $, respectively, where $$ \\sigma_{G}(T,t)=\\sigma_{G w}(T,t)+\\sigma_{G b}(T,t) $$",
      "source_page": 834,
      "source_pages": [
        834
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b4",
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b5"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          288.0,
          390.0,
          1058.0,
          437.0
        ],
        [
          534.0,
          457.0,
          812.0,
          481.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "625d45c1ce8738d9a212735b9723b08ef24a96a865467cffaf329f08527a206f"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The among-family covariance in generation t is the covariance between sibs from a parent in generation t - 1 $$ \\sigma_{Gb}(T,t)=\\sigma_{G}(T,t,t-1) $$",
      "source_page": 834,
      "source_pages": [
        834
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b7",
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b8"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          288.0,
          501.0,
          1058.0,
          547.0
        ],
        [
          562.0,
          547.0,
          785.0,
          570.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "f8da94b90fec1a55f109986a7bb610db4416630087ef2c36de7ea1f4111715a7"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The within-family genetic covariance follows as $$ \\begin{aligned}\\sigma_{Gw}(T,t)&=\\sigma_{G}(T,t)-\\sigma_{Gb}(T,t)\\\\&=\\sigma_{G}(T,t,t)-\\sigma_{G}(T,t,t-1)\\end{aligned} $$",
      "source_page": 834,
      "source_pages": [
        834
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b10",
        "Evolution_chapter23:p028:b11"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          289.0,
          582.0,
          702.0,
          606.0
        ],
        [
          506.0,
          626.0,
          839.0,
          679.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "42e2a70808ea3a62274d4c97c045660ac76c105f62a5dc3eeb1d6f5959617e77"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "For more general families, $ t - 1 $ is replaced by $ t - j $ when the last common ancestor to the family occurred $ j $ generations before the collection of families was scored. Note that the within- and among-family genetic variances in generation $ t $ are given by $ \\sigma_{Gw}(t, t) $ and $ \\sigma_{Gb}(t, t) $, respectively. Recalling Equation 23.8b, this implies a phenotypic variance for the among-family means of $ \\sigma_{\\overline{z}}(t, t) = \\sigma_{Gb}(t, t) + \\sigma_{e}^2 $.",
      "source_page": 834,
      "source_pages": [
        834
